   "html_text": "However, while Cohen’s interests and views evolved over the course of his career, his philosophy from all three periods nevertheless exhibits points of deep continuity. All of Cohen’s major works share a profoundly historical orientation. A concern with the history of philosophy dominates his writing, and he was convinced of history’s continuing significance for philosophy in the present. But he was also concerned with the histories of those subjects he took to be philosophy’s topics, including ",
